=========== какие флаги умеет эта версия ===========
Tests one or more proxy configurations. 
By default, if no flag is provided, it will wait for a single config link from standard input.
Use --from-db to test configs from the database library.
Usage:
  xray-knife http [flags]
  xray-knife http [command]
Available Commands:
  list-results Lists the results from the last HTTP test run from the database
Flags:
      --amount uint                   Download and upload amount (KB) (default 10000)
      --bind string                   Bind outbound dials to a specific OS interface (e.g. eth0). Linux: needs CAP_NET_RAW.
  -b, --body                          Show response body
      --check-preset string           Test each config against a diverse endpoint panel instead of one URL. Presets: cloudflare, global, google, gstatic, streaming
  -c, --config string                 The xray config link
  -z, --core string                   Core type (auto, singbox, xray) (default "auto")
      --dedup-semantic                Deduplicate by connection identity (protocol/address/port/credential/transport/TLS) instead of exact link text; drops re-skinned duplicates. Use --dedup-semantic=false for exact-string dedup only (default true)
  -f, --file string                   Read config links from a file
      --from-db                       Test configs from the database
  -h, --help                          help for http
  -e, --insecure                      Insecure tls connection (fake SNI)
      --interval uint16               Interval between pings in milliseconds (ms) (default 1000)
      --limit int                     Limit the number of configs to test from the DB (0 for all)
      --max-passed uint16             Stop the batch test after N configs pass (0 = test all). Ideal for large lists.
  -d, --mdelay uint16                 Maximum allowed delay (ms) (default 5000)
  -m, --method string                 Http method (default "GET")
  -o, --out string                    Output file for valid/all config links (default "valid.txt")
      --ping                          Enable continuous HTTP ping mode for a single config
      --prescan                       TCP pre-check: drop unreachable endpoints before the full test (much faster on large lists)
      --prescan-timeout uint16        TCP dial timeout for --prescan (ms) (default 2000)
      --prescan-workers uint16        Concurrent TCP dials for --prescan (default 512)
      --protocol string               Filter configs by protocol (vmess, vless, etc.) from the DB
      --retries uint16                Number of retries for failed proxy tests
      --rip                           Receive real IP (csv) (default true)
      --save-db                       Save test results to the database
      --sort                          Sort config links by their delay (fast to slow) in file output (default true)
  -S, --speedtest                     Speed test with speed.cloudflare.com
      --speedtest-timeout uint16      Time budget for each speedtest direction (seconds). Raise it for slow links or a large --amount. (default 30)
      --sub-id int                    Filter configs by subscription ID from the DB
      --test-urls string              Comma-separated URLs to test each config against (overrides --check-preset and --url). generate_204 URLs require a 204 response.
  -t, --threads uint16                Number of threads (default 50)
      --timeout uint16                HTTP client timeout in ms (0 = use mdelay value)
  -x, --type string                   Output type for file (csv, txt) (default "txt")
  -u, --url string                    The url to test config (single-endpoint mode) (default "https://cloudflare.com/cdn-cgi/trace")
      --url-success-threshold float   Fraction of panel endpoints that must succeed for a 'passed' grade (e.g. 0.75). Above 0 but below it grades 'semi-passed'. (default 1)
  -v, --verbose                       Verbose
Global Flags:
      --db string   Path to the xray-knife SQLite database (default: $XRAY_KNIFE_HOME/xray-knife.db, else ~/.xray-knife/xray-knife.db)
Use "xray-knife http [command] --help" for more information about a command.
